| Market/limit order semantics   | Market orders (fill at next available price) and limit      |
|                                | orders (price ceiling/floor)                                |
| Explicit fill timestamps       | latency_bars = 1 is currently metadata — must become a      |
|                                | checked, simulated fill time                                |
| Latency measurement            | Simulate realistic fill delay based on order type and       |
|                                | market conditions                                           |

-----------------------------------------------------------------
PHASE 3: Build Execution Accounting
-----------------------------------------------------------------

Per the audit's "Missing for serious paper trading" list:

| Component                    | Description                                           |
|------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| Cash/margin accounting       | Track cash balance, buying power, margin requirements|
| Position reconciliation      | Internal positions must match filled orders exactly  |
| P&L attribution              | Realized + unrealized P&L, decomposed by symbol       |
| Exchange-hours checks        | Only fill orders during simulated market hours        |
| Stale quote/data handling    | Detect and handle stale market data (no fills on     |
|                              | stale quotes)                                         |
| Retry logic                  | Handle transient failures gracefully                 |
| Audit trail                  | Immutable log of every order event (submission, fill, |
|                              | cancel, reject)                                       |
| Persistent kill-switch state | Kill switch must survive process restarts            |
| Alerting                     | Notify on gate breaches, rejections, data staleness  |
| Failure/restart tests        | Verify recovery from crash mid-execution             |


-----------------------------------------------------------------
PHASE 4: Wire Safeguards into the Order Flow
-----------------------------------------------------------------

Currently Safeguards is a standalone class that nobody calls.
The PaperBroker.submit() method must:

1. Check safeguards.check_position(intended) — reject if over limit.
2. Check safeguards.check_daily_loss(daily_return) — trip kill switch
   if breached.
3. Check safeguards.check_drawdown(current_drawdown) — trip kill switch
   if breached.
4. Check safeguards.check_data_freshness(last_bar_ts, now) — reject if
   data stale.
5. Only proceed with fill if ALL safeguards pass.
6. If kill switch is active, reject all new orders until manually
   reset.


-----------------------------------------------------------------
PHASE 5: Build the Paper Validation Framework
-----------------------------------------------------------------

The promotion state machine has:
PAPER_READY -> PAPER_VALIDATED -> LIVE_ELIGIBLE

The code explicitly states these are "deliberately not automatable here."
You need to define:

| State           | Entry Criteria                                                |
|-----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
| PAPER_READY     | All research gates pass + paper broker hardened + safeguards  |
|                 | wired                                                         |
| PAPER_VALIDATED | Minimum N days of continuous paper execution with: no         |
|                 | safeguard breaches, position reconciliation holds, P&L        |
|                 | attribution matches, kill switch tested                       |
| LIVE_ELIGIBLE   | Extended paper validation (typically 1-3 months) +            |
|                 | operational readiness review                                  |

Build:
- A paper-validation runner that executes the strategy against
  live/delayed market data.
- A paper-validation report that feeds evidence back into the
  promotion gate.
- Integration with the registry/leaderboard so paper evidence is
  recorded alongside research evidence.


-----------------------------------------------------------------
PHASE 6: Operational Readiness
-----------------------------------------------------------------

| Task                         | Why                                                    |
|------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|
| Failure/restart tests        | Verify the system recovers correctly from crashes     |
| Data feed integration        | Connect to a real market data feed (delayed is fine   |
|                              | for paper)                                             |
| Monitoring dashboard         | Real-time view of positions, P&L, safeguard status     |
| Manual override capability   | Ability to cancel all orders, flatten positions, reset |
|                              | kill switch                                            |
| Configuration validation     | Ensure paper-trading config is valid before launch    |
| Audit trail verification     | Confirm the audit trail is complete and tamper-evident|


-----------------------------------------------------------------
Recommended Execution Order
-----------------------------------------------------------------

1. Fix the strategy -> pass all 4 failed research gates -> reach
   ROBUST_OOS.
2. Harden PaperBroker (order lifecycle, validation, fill simulation).
3. Wire Safeguards into the order flow.
4. Build execution accounting (cash, positions, P&L).
5. Build paper validation framework (PAPER_READY -> PAPER_VALIDATED).
6. Operational readiness (failure tests, monitoring, overrides).
7. Launch paper trading.


-----------------------------------------------------------------
CRITICAL NOTE
-----------------------------------------------------------------

Phase 1 is the gating item. With a net Sharpe of -0.0712 and 4 failed
gates, paper trading would be trading a strategy that the system has
already determined is statistically indistinguishable from noise. The
honest path is to fix the signal first, then build the paper
infrastructure around a strategy that actually survives research gates.
</file>

